    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0819" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.288M/1–548: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-01-05T12:00:00+08:00">January 5,
                            1948—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 5—5:53 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. We consider that closing office at Changchun would have adverse effect on
                    public morale, thus further weakening Government position Changchun-Kirin area.
                    (ReDeptel 1586, December 31.) Siebens<anchor n="3" xml:id="d710-f1"/> has
                    expressed to Embassy his desire to remain Changchun even in the event it falls
                    to Communists. We feel that he should be allowed to remain and in the event the
                    city falls we would thereby have some indication of what the Communist attitude
                    would be toward American Consular offices in other areas of China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d710-f1" n="3" xml:id="d710-f1-content">
                <p>Allen C. Siebens, Vice Consul at Changchun.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
